# Design System Architecture

This rule defines the core architecture and technical foundation of our design system.

## Tech Stack
- Next.js App Router for routing and application framework
- React for component development
- TypeScript for type safety
- TailwindCSS for styling
- shadcn/ui as component foundation
- MDX for documentation
- Radix UI primitives for accessible foundations

## Project Structure
```
/app
  /api        # API routes
  /components # Core components
  /(routes)   # App routes using Next.js conventions
/components   
  /ui         # shadcn/ui components
  /primitives # Base primitive components
/lib          # Utility functions and shared logic
/styles       # Global styles and Tailwind config
/types        # TypeScript type definitions
/config       # Configuration files
  tokens.json # Design tokens
  theme.json  # Theme configuration
```

## Key Principles
- Minimal but extensible architecture
- Clear separation of concerns
- Type safety throughout
- Performance-focused bundling
- Scalable folder structure
- Maintainable code organization

## Best Practices
- Use Next.js App Router conventions
- Implement proper TypeScript types
- Follow component-driven development
- Maintain clean code architecture
- Use proper import/export patterns
- Keep bundle size optimized
